content.text:
Parent review rejects the current parity test because eval only returns scripted outcomes; it does not interpret the command, mutate state, or prove native readback.

Replace that parity mock with a real test-owned positional-protocol interpreter:
- parse condition count/types/key indexes/expected values from args;
- evaluate against test-owned state;
- on conflict return 0 with no mutations;
- parse mutation count and apply Set/Remove to a copied state, then commit and return 1;
- TTL may be parsed/ignored for this non-expiry sequence, but consume its arg correctly;
- no JSON, unsafe casts, non-null assertions, or production exports. Test-owned Map/loops are acceptable for provider simulation if all indexed values are decoded with Effect Schema rather than asserted.
- client get/set/del must use the same state.
